WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.240
"Dietary Approach to Naturally
Treating Menopause Symptoms"

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.400
There is a great
variety of symptoms

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.720
suffered by women
undergoing menopause.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.120
There are the so-called
vasomotor symptoms,

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.880
like night sweats and hot
ﬂashes, diﬃculty sleeping

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.800
or full-on insomnia, vaginal
dryness, and pain during sex,

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:29.040
as well as adverse effects on mood
including full-blown depression.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.800
Might exercise help?

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.760
Exercise can certainly help with
physical and psychological quality

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.800
of life in general, but unfortunately
there was no evidence

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:41.120
for the eﬀects of exercise on
menopause-speciﬁc symptoms.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.920
You know researchers are
getting desperate when they try

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.600
to see if giving people
pig placenta will help.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.720
Spoiler alert: it doesn’t.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.920
Well, we know oxidative stress,
which is a consequence of

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:58.000
excessive free oxygen radicals
or impaired antioxidant defense,

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.440
is linked not only to diseases

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:02.720
such as diabetes, obesity,
and cardiovascular disease,

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.000
but also menopausal
symptoms like hot flashes.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.800
Low free oxygen radical
defense is associated with

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.920
more menopausal symptoms,
just like having a diet with more

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:16.000
antioxidants is associated
with fewer menopausal symptoms.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.640
In fact, a high intake of
fruits and vegetables may delay

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.200
the onset of menopause
in the first place,

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.280
thought to be because
the presence of antioxidants

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.680
in fruits and vegetables may
counteract the adverse effects

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:28.800
of free radicals on the number
of functional eggs you still have

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.840
in your ovaries, whereas
a reason high meat consumption

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.720
has been related to
degenerative diseases

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.960
may not just be the
saturated fat and cholesterol,

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.840
but the pro-oxidation products
generated during their production,

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.520
storage, digestion,
and metabolism of meat.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:48.320
Similarly, since a pro-
inflammatory diet has also been

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:51.360
associated with higher menopause-
specific somatic symptoms,

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.343
meaning like hot flashes
and sleep issues,

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.520
that would mean moving
towards a more plant-based diet

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:00.560
packed with anti-inflammatory
components like fiber

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.960
and away from pro-inflammatory
foods containing

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:04.640
saturated fat and cholesterol.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:07.200
No wonder whole plant
foods intake has been

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.563
associated with fewer
menopausal symptoms.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:14.640
In terms of specific foods,
poultry and skim dairy products

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:18.240
may be particularly bad,
whereas soy milk seemed to help.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.560
So, women may derive benefit
from lower consumption

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.360
of poultry and skimmed dairy
and a greater consumption

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.280
of vegetables and soy milk.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.320
You don’t really know, though...
until you put it to the test.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.440
And indeed, women randomized
to drink soy milk reduced

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:35.698
their menopausal symptoms by
20 percent within 12 weeks.

00:02:35.698 --> 00:02:38.240
No wonder that those eating
strictly plant-based diets

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:41.040
report less bothersome
menopausal symptoms.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.880
Among women undergoing menopause,

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:45.360
vegans reported less
bothersome symptoms,

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.360
and within the diet
groups more vegetables,

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.560
and in the meat-eating group,
less ﬂesh food was associated

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.640
with less bothersome
symptoms as well.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:55.520
So, eating a plant-based
diet may be helpful for women

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:59.440
in their menopausal transition
who prefer a natural means

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:02.093
to manage their symptoms,
consistent with all the other

00:03:02.093 --> 00:03:05.440
studies demonstrating reduced
menopausal symptoms in those

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:09.920
consuming greater quantities of
plant-based foods and less meat.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:12.560
But again, maybe
there are other reasons

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.560
healthier eaters
have fewer symptoms.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:20.720
You can’t prove cause and
effect until...you guessed it.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:23.200
An interventional trial to
see if changing your diet

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.960
actually reduces symptoms.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:28.160
And in this study, where women
were encouraged to decrease fat

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:30.720
and increase fruit, vegetable,
and whole grain intake,

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.840
they were significantly
more likely to eliminate

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.200
their vasomotor symptoms like
hot flashes and night sweats

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.800
compared to the control group.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.520
So, it’s certainly not all or nothing.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.240
And within a plant-based
diet, those randomized

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:47.040
to a meat-free diet with
daily flaxseed oil, walnuts,

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.600
and almonds did better
than those randomized

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.880
to the same diet but with
daily extra-virgin olive oil.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.760
After 16 weeks, the
vegetarian diet that was rich

00:03:55.760 --> 00:04:00.160
in omega-3s did better reducing
vasomotor symptom frequency.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:03.200
In fact, even just two teaspoons
worth of ground flaxseeds a day

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:07.600
alone can significantly decrease
menopausal symptoms to about

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.640
the same extent as
hormone replacement therapy,

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:13.840
but without the side effects.

